  "live_records": {
    "q-88948": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88948",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an estimate for the population mean.\n\n$$\n7,\\,-3,\\,-6,\\,9,\\,5\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(7-3-6+9+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5} \\\\  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
